commit cbc19a380bc03b14d5ca2999cd798b7c76a8c230

C03: a completed private-memory save says what it remembered, as local memory, in the request's language (MEMORY1249 repair)

The completion facts of memory.save carried only flags (saved/corrected/
sensitive/replayed) and the composer read them as prose — «el archivo fue
guardado… ni acciones de replay» — while the language came from the closed
reply «confirmar» (MEMORY1247). The projection now adds `remembered` (the
non-secret value the person just stated) and drops false flags; the session
publishes the completion against the original request text; the composer is
told the datum lives in the private local memory, not a file. No tests
(owner order).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>


